# Phase 6: Borate-Inspired Refined Candidates
# Goal: Maintain high SEI homogeneity while passing Tier 1/2 viability
# Strategy: Reduce structural complexity of borate esters, use simpler F-rich carbonates

# === Simple Fluorinated Carbonates (best homogeneity without failing Tier 1) ===
COC(=O)OC(F)(F)C(F)(F)F
COC(=O)OC(F)(F)F
CCOC(=O)OC(F)(F)F
COC(=O)OC(F)F
CCOC(=O)OCC(F)F
COC(=O)OCC(F)F

# === Simplified Borate Analogs (lower complexity boron structures) ===
# Cyclic borate with single fluorinated chain
O1B(OCC(F)F)(OCC)OC1

# Cyclic borate with methoxy substituents (simpler)
COC(=O)OB1OC(C)(OCC(F)F)O1

# Boron tri-fluoride analog (not a real borate but tests the concept)
F[B](F)(F)

# === Highly Fluorinated Simple Carbonates ===
# Perfluoro-isopropyl methyl carbonate
COC(=O)OC(F)(C(F)F)F

# Trifluoro-ethyl methyl carbonate
COC(=O)OCC(F)(F)F

# Difluoro-methyl ethyl carbonate
CCOC(=O)OC(F)F

# === Dual-Functional Fluoro-Unsaturated (from Phase 1, verified valid) ===
COC(=O)OCC=C
COC(=O)OC(F)C=C
COC(=O)C(F)=C(F)F
FCC(F)(F)S(=O)(=O)OC=C
